1
00:00:00,425 --> 00:00:05,465
This series is a work of fiction inspired
by questions that arise within the human heart.

2
00:00:05,485 --> 00:00:09,865
It is not intended to offend or pass judgment
on any beliefs, religions, or individuals.

3
00:00:10,185 --> 00:00:13,005
You’re going on to the seminary
with Kongdech, right?

4
00:00:13,155 --> 00:00:14,155
Right?

5
00:00:16,665 --> 00:00:18,225
And where did your rosary go?

6
00:00:18,875 --> 00:00:20,305
I don’t know where I left it.

7
00:00:21,315 --> 00:00:22,315
I ran into Barth.

8
00:00:23,565 --> 00:00:24,805
He dropped it.

9
00:00:25,165 --> 00:00:26,505
He must be suspicious about us.

10
00:00:26,775 --> 00:00:28,005
Calm down. It’s nothing.

11
00:00:31,835 --> 00:00:34,405
I’m tired. And I’m scared.

12
00:00:34,835 --> 00:00:36,205
And I’m not happy at all.

13
00:00:36,685 --> 00:00:38,205
I’m asking you seriously, Tanrak.

14
00:00:38,655 --> 00:00:40,305
That calling from God you hear,

15
00:00:40,565 --> 00:00:42,045
is it still as loud as it used to be?

16
00:00:43,165 --> 00:00:46,305
I’m in love even though I know it’s wrong.

17
00:00:46,695 --> 00:00:48,625
If this place isn’t for us,

18
00:00:49,045 --> 00:00:50,345
let's run away together.

19
00:00:53,745 --> 00:00:57,435
FOR HIS ANGER LASTS ONLY A MOMENT,
BUT HIS FAVOR LASTS A LIFETIME;

20
00:00:57,465 --> 00:01:01,635
WEEPING MAY STAY FOR THE NIGHT,
BUT REJOICING COMES IN THE MORNING.

21
00:01:01,655 --> 00:01:02,715
PSALM 30:5

22
00:01:39,305 --> 00:01:40,905
Looks like the power’s been cut off.

23
00:01:41,915 --> 00:01:43,405
There are some candles over there,

24
00:01:43,445 --> 00:01:44,485
if I remember right.

25
00:01:44,665 --> 00:01:45,665
Try looking around.

26
00:01:51,965 --> 00:01:53,505
I'll look in the kitchen.

27
00:02:58,915 --> 00:02:59,915
Found one.

28
00:03:22,255 --> 00:03:23,255
What are you doing?

29
00:03:25,345 --> 00:03:26,485
Beloved.

30
00:03:30,085 --> 00:03:31,085
It’s mine.

31
00:03:32,775 --> 00:03:34,355
I’ve probably had it since I was a kid.

32
00:03:40,905 --> 00:03:42,605
B, is this your name?

33
00:03:44,835 --> 00:03:46,145
My mom had it made.

34
00:03:49,965 --> 00:03:51,005
Beloved.

35
00:03:54,615 --> 00:03:55,615
My mom…

36
00:03:56,635 --> 00:03:58,625
has called me “beloved”
since I was little.

37
00:04:04,305 --> 00:04:05,305
Put it on.

38
00:04:06,255 --> 00:04:07,255
It looks cool.

39
00:04:20,365 --> 00:04:21,505
I think…

40
00:04:21,705 --> 00:04:24,305
God probably won’t forgive me
anytime soon.

41
00:04:30,585 --> 00:04:31,585
Me neither.

42
00:04:38,545 --> 00:04:40,305
Hey, don’t get all serious.

43
00:04:40,865 --> 00:04:41,865
Hm.

44
00:04:43,165 --> 00:04:45,125
Right now, if you’re gonna stress
about something,

45
00:04:45,615 --> 00:04:47,555
stress about having no underwear.

46
00:04:48,515 --> 00:04:49,955
You forgot to bring any, didn’t you?

47
00:04:54,215 --> 00:04:55,215
Here.

48
00:04:56,485 --> 00:04:57,705
Take mine for now.

49
00:04:58,545 --> 00:04:59,545
But…

50
00:05:00,545 --> 00:05:02,105
it might be a little loose on you.

51
00:05:03,135 --> 00:05:04,135
Let’s measure.

52
00:05:04,275 --> 00:05:05,005
Hey!

53
00:05:05,085 --> 00:05:08,255
Will it fit? Can you wear it?

54
00:05:08,485 --> 00:05:09,485
Give it.

55
00:05:09,745 --> 00:05:11,225
Hey, Tan, you have to measure first.

56
00:05:11,255 --> 00:05:12,085
Measure what?

57
00:05:12,155 --> 00:05:12,955
We have to measure.

58
00:05:12,985 --> 00:05:14,605
How else would we know if it fits?

59
00:05:15,275 --> 00:05:16,405
How would we know?

60
00:05:16,775 --> 00:05:17,775
Don’t.

61
00:05:17,945 --> 00:05:19,165
We have to measure first.

62
00:05:19,185 --> 00:05:20,605
How else would we know?

63
00:05:20,850 --> 00:05:22,705
Give it here. Those are mine.

64
00:05:37,745 --> 00:05:38,745
Tan…

65
00:05:44,135 --> 00:05:45,205
right now

66
00:05:45,845 --> 00:05:46,885
can we…

67
00:05:47,365 --> 00:05:49,225
not think about anything else?

68
00:05:50,755 --> 00:05:51,905
Let it all go for now.

69
00:05:54,075 --> 00:05:55,205
Just…

70
00:05:56,345 --> 00:05:58,205
having you here with me is enough.

71
00:06:09,935 --> 00:06:10,935
Well…

72
00:06:11,605 --> 00:06:13,005
I’m here with you, aren’t I?

73
00:07:41,905 --> 00:07:42,905
Here.

74
00:07:43,485 --> 00:07:44,705
Proudly presenting.

75
00:07:48,425 --> 00:07:50,705
Whoa, Barth.

76
00:07:51,235 --> 00:07:54,405
Did you toast this bread or burn it?

77
00:07:57,055 --> 00:07:58,885
This is called crispy outside,
soft on the inside.

78
00:07:58,905 --> 00:07:59,905
Come on.

79
00:08:01,155 --> 00:08:02,705
I went out and bought it for you.

80
00:08:03,295 --> 00:08:05,205
Not even a tiny thank-you?

81
00:08:07,175 --> 00:08:08,755
Aww…

82
00:08:09,695 --> 00:08:10,665
Thank youuu.

83
00:08:10,695 --> 00:08:11,305
Hey.

84
00:08:11,485 --> 00:08:13,005
You’ll get it on me.

85
00:08:13,055 --> 00:08:14,755
- Thank you.
- You’ll get it on me, Tanrak.

86
00:08:14,955 --> 00:08:16,005
It’ll smear.

87
00:08:16,535 --> 00:08:17,535
Come on, eat.

88
00:08:19,935 --> 00:08:20,935
Here.

89
00:08:25,735 --> 00:08:27,205
Tanrak, I made this for you.

90
00:08:29,155 --> 00:08:31,005
Here, I got you this too.

91
00:08:49,095 --> 00:08:50,485
Eat it before it warms up.

92
00:09:11,655 --> 00:09:14,405
You eat this better than anyone
I’ve ever met.

93
00:09:15,215 --> 00:09:16,215
It’s good.

94
00:09:17,225 --> 00:09:18,605
Twice as good.

95
00:09:19,205 --> 00:09:20,205
Here.

96
00:09:25,205 --> 00:09:26,205
Can I have some?

97
00:09:42,125 --> 00:09:44,005
So…

98
00:09:47,015 --> 00:09:48,875
what song would Nong Tanrak like to hear?

99
00:09:50,025 --> 00:09:51,025
I don’t know.

100
00:09:51,295 --> 00:09:52,295
You pick.

101
00:09:57,125 --> 00:09:59,305
Then today, DJ P'Barth…

102
00:09:59,555 --> 00:10:01,225
will play a song for Nong Tanrak.

103
00:10:02,475 --> 00:10:03,505
Just now

104
00:10:03,975 --> 00:10:06,505
what were you thinking about?

105
00:10:13,645 --> 00:10:14,645
I don’t know.

106
00:10:14,955 --> 00:10:17,905
I guess I was thinking about my parents.

107
00:10:32,745 --> 00:10:33,605
Then…

108
00:10:33,755 --> 00:10:35,305
should we go to your house today?

109
00:10:38,055 --> 00:10:39,605
My house was sold.

110
00:10:41,445 --> 00:10:44,105
But if we want to go somewhere
that’ll make me miss them less,

111
00:10:44,485 --> 00:10:46,005
there is one other place.

112
00:10:57,385 --> 00:11:01,625
ST. PEDRO CHURCH CEMETERY GATE

113
00:11:07,815 --> 00:11:09,685
Man, we shouldn’t have missed
the 1 p.m. bus.

114
00:11:13,735 --> 00:11:14,735
Tanrak.

115
00:11:16,345 --> 00:11:17,945
Are you Pracha’s son, Tanrak?

116
00:11:19,455 --> 00:11:20,805
Yes, I am.

117
00:11:22,465 --> 00:11:23,605
It’s me, Lek.

118
00:11:28,415 --> 00:11:29,805
I almost didn’t recognize you.

119
00:11:30,145 --> 00:11:30,935
Hello, Auntie Lek.

120
00:11:30,955 --> 00:11:31,705
Hello.

121
00:11:31,905 --> 00:11:32,505
Hello.

122
00:11:32,655 --> 00:11:33,655
Hello.

123
00:11:34,735 --> 00:11:36,405
Did you only just have time to come?

124
00:11:36,585 --> 00:11:38,545
I didn’t see you
at last year’s cemetery blessing.

125
00:11:39,875 --> 00:11:42,805
Last year, I had to go
to military cadet camp.

126
00:11:42,875 --> 00:11:44,305
So I couldn’t make it.

127
00:11:45,835 --> 00:11:47,515
Have you paid respects
to your parents yet?

128
00:11:49,895 --> 00:11:50,895
Not yet.

129
00:11:52,065 --> 00:11:53,505
The cemetery’s closed now.

130
00:11:54,265 --> 00:11:57,585
Are you heading back,
or coming back tomorrow?

131
00:12:01,985 --> 00:12:03,605
I haven’t thought that far.

132
00:12:04,035 --> 00:12:06,085
If I can’t find a place to stay,

133
00:12:06,515 --> 00:12:08,205
I’ll probably have to come another day.

134
00:12:08,675 --> 00:12:09,805
Then how about this?

135
00:12:09,965 --> 00:12:11,805
Stay at my place tonight.

136
00:12:12,035 --> 00:12:13,795
I’ll bring you back tomorrow morning.

137
00:12:20,245 --> 00:12:21,245
That'd be great.

138
00:12:21,705 --> 00:12:23,675
LEK’S LAUNDRY SERVICE

139
00:12:24,085 --> 00:12:25,285
Come on in, boys.

140
00:12:32,115 --> 00:12:33,505
The house is a little messy.

141
00:13:01,045 --> 00:13:02,045
That’s me.

142
00:13:02,855 --> 00:13:03,915
In both pictures.

143
00:13:15,685 --> 00:13:16,755
Dear Lord,

144
00:13:16,885 --> 00:13:18,825
please bless us

145
00:13:18,855 --> 00:13:20,805
and the food we are about to receive.

146
00:13:22,055 --> 00:13:23,735
In the name of the Father,

147
00:13:23,765 --> 00:13:24,505
and of the Son,

148
00:13:24,545 --> 00:13:25,825
and of the Holy Spirit. Amen.

149
00:13:27,315 --> 00:13:29,005
Eat up. You’re hungry, aren’t you?

150
00:13:29,365 --> 00:13:30,365
Go on.

151
00:13:32,335 --> 00:13:33,005
So…

152
00:13:33,225 --> 00:13:34,885
What was Tanrak like as a kid?

153
00:13:35,345 --> 00:13:36,845
Was he as talkative as he is now?

154
00:13:37,475 --> 00:13:38,715
How young are we talking?

155
00:13:39,095 --> 00:13:41,205
I’ve known him
since he was in an incubator.

156
00:13:42,025 --> 00:13:43,775
As a baby, he cried all the time.

157
00:13:43,945 --> 00:13:45,505
But as he got older,

158
00:13:46,245 --> 00:13:47,245
he got quieter.

159
00:13:47,735 --> 00:13:48,915
He just hid behind his dad.

160
00:13:49,605 --> 00:13:53,155
How did you know Tanrak’s family?

161
00:13:54,505 --> 00:13:58,305
I was friends with Tanrak’s dad
since we were in secondary school.

162
00:13:59,485 --> 00:14:00,735
We went to the same school

163
00:14:01,175 --> 00:14:03,505
and became really close.

164
00:14:04,065 --> 00:14:05,905
Oh, I remember now.

165
00:14:06,345 --> 00:14:07,505
I have photos too.

166
00:14:13,825 --> 00:14:14,825
Ta-da.

167
00:14:26,815 --> 00:14:29,515
Auntie Lek, did you live
in Magdalene House too?

168
00:14:29,775 --> 00:14:30,775
I did.

169
00:14:30,805 --> 00:14:32,795
We started together back in Grade 7.

170
00:14:43,105 --> 00:14:44,665
In Grade 12,

171
00:14:44,845 --> 00:14:48,405
we were still hiding under blankets
studying for exams together.

172
00:14:55,015 --> 00:15:00,605
Did the rector know
you and my dad were going to leave?

173
00:15:01,145 --> 00:15:02,145
Of course.

174
00:15:04,025 --> 00:15:05,305
Father knew everything.

175
00:15:06,205 --> 00:15:07,805
He just chose to look the other way.

176
00:15:09,005 --> 00:15:10,475
I knew I had to leave either way.

177
00:15:13,855 --> 00:15:17,105
I knew I wanted to be a woman
ever since I was little.

178
00:15:19,175 --> 00:15:21,205
I couldn’t keep going down that path.

179
00:15:28,485 --> 00:15:29,485
So…

180
00:15:30,365 --> 00:15:31,805
how did you feel

181
00:15:33,235 --> 00:15:34,465
when you left?

182
00:15:34,705 --> 00:15:36,205
Well…

183
00:15:37,885 --> 00:15:38,965
I did wonder.

184
00:15:39,655 --> 00:15:42,205
I wondered if, after leaving,

185
00:15:43,415 --> 00:15:45,145
God would still love me.

186
00:15:46,395 --> 00:15:47,905
But in the end, here I am.

187
00:15:50,435 --> 00:15:52,605
I can still love Him just the same.

188
00:16:00,875 --> 00:16:01,875
Eat up.

189
00:16:02,325 --> 00:16:03,605
You’re hungry, aren’t you?

190
00:16:06,495 --> 00:16:07,805
Eat some more.

191
00:16:09,995 --> 00:16:10,995
I bet

192
00:16:11,525 --> 00:16:12,905
you had

193
00:16:13,945 --> 00:16:16,705
a lot of friends at Magdalene House.

194
00:16:17,595 --> 00:16:18,705
A whole gang of us.

195
00:16:20,875 --> 00:16:22,305
Know who the ringleader was?

196
00:16:23,645 --> 00:16:24,645
Your dad.

197
00:16:39,535 --> 00:16:40,705
Here you go.

198
00:16:43,265 --> 00:16:44,305
Thank you, Auntie Lek.

199
00:16:45,515 --> 00:16:47,405
They’ve been packed away.
I hardly use them.

200
00:16:48,105 --> 00:16:50,355
Want to make the bed now? I can help.

201
00:16:50,705 --> 00:16:51,905
Oh, it’s okay.

202
00:16:52,185 --> 00:16:54,305
Barth and I can do it together.

203
00:16:57,145 --> 00:16:58,145
Barth.

204
00:16:58,175 --> 00:17:00,085
Come help me make the bed.

205
00:17:10,245 --> 00:17:11,255
This Barth…

206
00:17:12,565 --> 00:17:13,905
is he your close friend?

207
00:17:14,955 --> 00:17:15,955
Oh.

208
00:17:16,435 --> 00:17:17,605
Yeah, we’re close.

209
00:17:19,455 --> 00:17:21,005
When you talk about him,

210
00:17:22,775 --> 00:17:24,805
you get this look in your eyes.

211
00:17:27,545 --> 00:17:28,545
Oh.

212
00:17:29,795 --> 00:17:30,905
It’s nothing.

213
00:17:36,875 --> 00:17:38,405
I’m not trying to tease you.

214
00:17:40,495 --> 00:17:42,005
I just see myself in you.

215
00:17:44,815 --> 00:17:47,585
I once looked at someone that way too.

216
00:17:57,025 --> 00:17:59,505
What did you do?

217
00:18:03,125 --> 00:18:04,505
I thought

218
00:18:06,605 --> 00:18:08,505
one day I’d be able to cut it out.

219
00:18:12,315 --> 00:18:13,405
Did you?

220
00:18:15,535 --> 00:18:17,505
I was young, you know.

221
00:18:20,105 --> 00:18:21,705
In the end, I couldn’t fight it.

222
00:18:24,985 --> 00:18:26,505
So you left?

223
00:18:37,545 --> 00:18:39,305
I blamed myself for a while.

224
00:18:41,345 --> 00:18:43,195
I thought I should’ve been stronger.

225
00:18:53,125 --> 00:18:54,405
But as I got older,

226
00:18:56,075 --> 00:18:58,205
I realized I’m only human.

227
00:19:07,005 --> 00:19:08,105
It’s…

228
00:19:10,175 --> 00:19:11,805
It’s really hard, Auntie Lek.

229
00:19:16,625 --> 00:19:17,905
That’s just life.

230
00:19:31,185 --> 00:19:32,805
But I’ve never hated myself.

231
00:19:36,465 --> 00:19:38,405
Even now, I’m still proud

232
00:19:40,055 --> 00:19:41,505
of the choice I made.

233
00:19:56,155 --> 00:19:58,505
Can I… hug you?

234
00:20:08,805 --> 00:20:10,205
If you can’t figure it out,

235
00:20:10,885 --> 00:20:12,505
you don’t have to right now.

236
00:20:21,735 --> 00:20:24,505
Just be honest with your own feelings.

237
00:20:29,265 --> 00:20:30,265
Okay?

238
00:20:35,435 --> 00:20:36,085
Okay.

239
00:20:36,245 --> 00:20:37,945
And things will get better.

240
00:20:50,585 --> 00:20:51,995
Auntie Lek seems

241
00:20:52,585 --> 00:20:54,425
really happy with her life, doesn’t she?

242
00:20:56,055 --> 00:20:59,005
When she talked about God,

243
00:21:00,055 --> 00:21:02,505
she didn’t seem sad

244
00:21:03,065 --> 00:21:04,105
or angry.

245
00:21:05,825 --> 00:21:07,795
She looked really happy.

246
00:21:18,435 --> 00:21:20,105
Someday, you’ll be like that too.

247
00:21:26,285 --> 00:21:27,305
Someday…

248
00:21:36,185 --> 00:21:37,305
do you think

249
00:21:40,035 --> 00:21:42,605
there’s a place up there
for the two of us?

250
00:22:11,305 --> 00:22:15,005
MARIA SAOWANEE SAWATDIRAKKUL

251
00:22:17,205 --> 00:22:22,035
PAOLO PRACHA SAWATDIRAKKUL

252
00:22:24,575 --> 00:22:26,205
Everything is so hard.

253
00:22:27,455 --> 00:22:32,105
Mom, Dad, are you still waiting
for Rak in heaven?

254
00:22:41,455 --> 00:22:42,505
Who’s Rak?

255
00:22:46,385 --> 00:22:47,385
Mind your business.

256
00:22:53,975 --> 00:22:55,105
Tanrak’s mom and dad,

257
00:22:56,415 --> 00:22:57,465
who’s Rak?

258
00:23:01,305 --> 00:23:04,205
When I was little,

259
00:23:05,175 --> 00:23:10,805
I called myself Rak with my parents.

260
00:23:14,055 --> 00:23:15,055
Really?

261
00:23:15,245 --> 00:23:16,405
Wow. Little Rak.

262
00:23:17,195 --> 00:23:18,305
Little Rak.

263
00:23:18,775 --> 00:23:20,605
Hey, don’t push it.

264
00:23:21,555 --> 00:23:22,885
My parents are watching.

265
00:23:28,755 --> 00:23:30,705
Try calling yourself Rak with me too.

266
00:23:32,475 --> 00:23:33,905
What, are you my parent?

267
00:23:34,455 --> 00:23:36,305
Why would I call myself Rak with you?

268
00:23:41,265 --> 00:23:42,505
I’m not.

269
00:23:43,945 --> 00:23:46,205
So how should I introduce myself
to your parents?

270
00:23:47,805 --> 00:23:48,805
Your boyfriend?

271
00:23:50,225 --> 00:23:51,225
Your lover?

272
00:23:52,565 --> 00:23:53,565
Your sweetheart?

273
00:23:55,295 --> 00:23:57,105
Or Rak’s sweetheart?

274
00:23:59,985 --> 00:24:02,915
“Rak’s sweetheart” sounds cute,
doesn’t it?

275
00:24:07,435 --> 00:24:08,905
Mom, Dad,

276
00:24:10,215 --> 00:24:11,215
this is…

277
00:24:12,155 --> 00:24:13,155
Barth.

278
00:24:14,515 --> 00:24:15,905
He’s kind of a jerk.

279
00:24:19,095 --> 00:24:20,095
Happy now?

280
00:24:25,935 --> 00:24:26,935
Ahem.

281
00:24:28,035 --> 00:24:29,205
Tanrak’s mom and dad,

282
00:24:30,515 --> 00:24:32,105
you don’t have to worry from now on.

283
00:24:32,675 --> 00:24:34,145
I’ll take care of Tanrak.

284
00:24:37,595 --> 00:24:39,305
You? Take care of me?

285
00:24:39,945 --> 00:24:41,805
I’m the one who has to take care of you.

286
00:24:42,915 --> 00:24:44,605
You can barely handle your own life.

287
00:24:46,265 --> 00:24:47,605
Hurry up. Help me with this.

288
00:24:50,025 --> 00:24:51,705
I can take care of you, Rak.

289
00:24:53,665 --> 00:24:54,665
Really?

290
00:24:55,835 --> 00:24:58,605
You even make me do your homework.

291
00:25:02,695 --> 00:25:04,135
I bring you along when I skip class.

292
00:25:11,115 --> 00:25:12,305
Come on, help me.

293
00:25:13,005 --> 00:25:14,505
I'm helping Rak.

294
00:25:26,125 --> 00:25:28,885
Auntie Lek, we have to go now.

295
00:25:30,685 --> 00:25:31,685
Wait a second.

296
00:25:40,275 --> 00:25:41,505
This is my number.

297
00:25:42,085 --> 00:25:43,525
Come visit again when you have time.

298
00:25:44,725 --> 00:25:45,725
I will.

299
00:25:45,905 --> 00:25:48,305
And this Bible

300
00:25:49,945 --> 00:25:52,475
belonged to your dad.
I borrowed it from him.

301
00:25:56,295 --> 00:25:58,105
It should be with you.

302
00:25:58,155 --> 00:25:59,595
PAOLO PRACHA SAWATDIRAKKUL

303
00:26:02,415 --> 00:26:03,505
Thank you, Auntie Lek.

304
00:26:04,585 --> 00:26:05,805
Thank you so much.

305
00:26:06,075 --> 00:26:07,505
I pray

306
00:26:07,625 --> 00:26:09,805
that God watches over you both.

307
00:26:13,935 --> 00:26:14,935
Thank you.

308
00:26:19,285 --> 00:26:20,405
Don’t forget,

309
00:26:21,625 --> 00:26:23,805
you can love God

310
00:26:25,035 --> 00:26:27,035
and love yourself at the same time.

311
00:26:37,915 --> 00:26:38,555
Goodbye.

312
00:26:38,835 --> 00:26:39,835
Goodbye.

313
00:26:40,295 --> 00:26:41,455
Have a safe trip.

314
00:26:42,045 --> 00:26:43,045
Yes.

315
00:26:48,705 --> 00:26:52,885
I've heard people say,
there's a place somewhere.

316
00:26:53,195 --> 00:26:56,705
A land like a beautiful dream
beyond compare.

317
00:26:56,835 --> 00:27:00,085
Where every soul lives endlessly.

318
00:27:01,235 --> 00:27:05,005
I used to dream one day
that’s where I’d be.

319
00:27:06,245 --> 00:27:14,205
But since the day I found you,
a brand-new world opened up for me.

320
00:27:14,705 --> 00:27:19,275
With you right here,
with us right here.

321
00:27:19,535 --> 00:27:23,005
There's nowhere else I'd rather be.

322
00:27:25,285 --> 00:27:27,585
Every second From that moment.

323
00:27:27,605 --> 00:27:29,868
That I have you near.

324
00:27:29,887 --> 00:27:33,835
Feels like I’ve found
the land of my dreams.

325
00:27:34,335 --> 00:27:39,505
My world turns so beautiful
I wanna stop the time.

326
00:27:39,685 --> 00:27:42,905
And hold this moment
for as long as I can.

327
00:27:42,945 --> 00:27:45,288
If heaven is real
If it’s not real

328
00:27:45,305 --> 00:27:47,404
how beautiful could it be.

329
00:27:47,715 --> 00:27:51,905
I’m not so sure if I need to see.

330
00:27:52,245 --> 00:27:57,005
As long as you’re the one here
standing next to me.

331
00:27:57,035 --> 00:28:02,595
If heaven doesn’t have you there,
that's not where I wanna be.

332
00:28:03,065 --> 00:28:06,505
I too have someone important
I want you to meet.

333
00:28:13,285 --> 00:28:14,485
Is your mom strict?

334
00:28:15,455 --> 00:28:18,915
What should I call her?

335
00:28:19,355 --> 00:28:21,305
Should I call her Auntie?

336
00:28:22,705 --> 00:28:25,285
Or just Barth’s mom?

337
00:28:26,615 --> 00:28:27,685
Call her whatever.

338
00:28:28,245 --> 00:28:29,245
My mom’s nice.

339
00:28:30,365 --> 00:28:31,905
Once she sees you’re Christian,

340
00:28:32,515 --> 00:28:33,515
you’ll be fine.

341
00:28:48,155 --> 00:28:49,205
What?

342
00:28:51,325 --> 00:28:54,805
Relatives of Ms. Busaya Tungwongwat,
you may see the inmate now.

343
00:28:56,525 --> 00:28:57,525
Let’s go.

344
00:29:30,175 --> 00:29:31,175
Barth.

345
00:29:35,275 --> 00:29:36,605
Is school out already?

346
00:29:36,965 --> 00:29:38,405
Or did you take a day off?

347
00:29:39,515 --> 00:29:41,505
It’s Founder's Day, Mom.

348
00:29:42,335 --> 00:29:44,705
The school brought us to Bangkok
on a field trip,

349
00:29:44,875 --> 00:29:46,305
so I asked to stop by and see you.

350
00:29:57,615 --> 00:29:59,005
Are you sick?

351
00:30:00,645 --> 00:30:02,785
There’s a flu outbreak in here.

352
00:30:02,815 --> 00:30:04,205
Is it spreading outside?

353
00:30:08,295 --> 00:30:09,505
I’m not sick, Mom.

354
00:30:10,505 --> 00:30:11,805
It’s just dusty.

355
00:30:12,615 --> 00:30:13,615
My nose hurts.

356
00:30:15,935 --> 00:30:18,505
Then rinse your nose with saline.

357
00:30:18,765 --> 00:30:20,405
Remember how I taught you?

358
00:30:22,255 --> 00:30:22,915
I know.

359
00:30:23,225 --> 00:30:24,305
I remember, Mom.

360
00:30:29,505 --> 00:30:30,205
Oh.

361
00:30:30,475 --> 00:30:31,475
Come here.

362
00:30:32,165 --> 00:30:33,705
This is Tanrak.

363
00:30:34,525 --> 00:30:36,265
He’s my friend from school.

364
00:30:37,575 --> 00:30:41,005
We came here together,
so I brought him to meet you.

365
00:30:43,705 --> 00:30:44,705
Hello.

366
00:30:45,095 --> 00:30:47,005
What a beautiful name. Tanrak.

367
00:30:48,755 --> 00:30:49,955
Did you just transfer there?

368
00:30:50,045 --> 00:30:51,305
You look unfamiliar.

369
00:30:58,825 --> 00:30:59,825
Yes.

370
00:31:00,965 --> 00:31:01,965
Barth’s mom.

371
00:31:03,445 --> 00:31:05,105
Just call me Mom.

372
00:31:10,095 --> 00:31:11,805
You’re Catholic too?

373
00:31:12,525 --> 00:31:13,555
That’s wonderful.

374
00:31:14,925 --> 00:31:16,885
Do you get to pray at school?

375
00:31:19,385 --> 00:31:21,105
Mom, what are you talking about now?

376
00:31:24,885 --> 00:31:26,505
Please look after Barth for me.

377
00:31:28,125 --> 00:31:30,105
With me in here, he must be lonely.

378
00:31:34,155 --> 00:31:35,805
He doesn’t have many friends either.

379
00:31:38,185 --> 00:31:39,625
When Barth went to school,

380
00:31:40,045 --> 00:31:42,905
he always came back and told me
everything that happened.

381
00:31:45,065 --> 00:31:46,705
Bad food, he'd complain.

382
00:31:47,565 --> 00:31:48,905
Strict teachers, he'd complain.

383
00:31:53,925 --> 00:31:55,005
It’s a shame.

384
00:32:00,275 --> 00:32:03,705
Tanrak,
listen to him complain for me, okay?

385
00:32:13,395 --> 00:32:14,805
Help each other study.

386
00:32:17,095 --> 00:32:18,705
Do you still stay up late?

387
00:32:20,605 --> 00:32:22,455
Mom, that was when I was little.

388
00:32:23,145 --> 00:32:24,305
I’m a grown-up now.

389
00:32:25,305 --> 00:32:26,075
I’m in Grade 12.

390
00:32:26,105 --> 00:32:29,305
Soon enough, I'll graduate.
Then I can work.

391
00:32:31,735 --> 00:32:34,105
You talk like I’m still a kid.

392
00:32:35,975 --> 00:32:37,105
Still nagging like always.

393
00:32:41,055 --> 00:32:42,905
You’ve always said you were grown up.

394
00:32:45,495 --> 00:32:48,005
You said the same thing when you were ten.

395
00:32:53,735 --> 00:32:55,285
You know how happy I am

396
00:32:56,185 --> 00:32:57,675
that you came to see me?

397
00:33:00,455 --> 00:33:01,905
Next time you have a day off,

398
00:33:02,515 --> 00:33:04,105
will you come again?

399
00:33:11,725 --> 00:33:12,725
I'm gonna go.

400
00:33:16,465 --> 00:33:17,465
Goodbye, Mom.

401
00:33:27,315 --> 00:33:29,605
Lawyer Kai came to see me the other day.

402
00:33:30,085 --> 00:33:33,105
He said the police found more evidence.

403
00:33:36,305 --> 00:33:37,505
What evidence?

404
00:33:38,975 --> 00:33:41,205
They dug up old incidents.

405
00:33:42,735 --> 00:33:46,305
Like that time he put me in the hospital.

406
00:33:46,945 --> 00:33:47,945
Remember?

407
00:33:50,455 --> 00:33:51,505
Actually,

408
00:33:52,485 --> 00:33:54,705
I should be the one in there,

409
00:33:56,455 --> 00:33:57,455
not you.

410
00:34:02,095 --> 00:34:04,305
If that happened,
how could I live with myself?

411
00:34:09,105 --> 00:34:11,105
Let me do my job as your mother.

412
00:34:16,995 --> 00:34:19,405
Uncle Kai said this time,

413
00:34:21,895 --> 00:34:25,405
the court may be sympathetic.

414
00:34:27,965 --> 00:34:30,205
I might be cleared of the charges.

415
00:34:30,975 --> 00:34:32,105
Or at least,

416
00:34:33,255 --> 00:34:36,205
I may have less than a year left.

417
00:34:41,165 --> 00:34:42,905
Pray for me, Barth.

418
00:34:45,725 --> 00:34:46,805
I’ll hang in there.

419
00:34:48,945 --> 00:34:50,485
You have to hang in there too.

420
00:34:55,585 --> 00:34:56,585
I'll…

421
00:34:58,335 --> 00:34:59,805
pray for you.

422
00:35:08,475 --> 00:35:10,405
When I get out, I’ll hug you.

423
00:35:13,885 --> 00:35:15,205
I love you.

424
00:35:22,725 --> 00:35:23,725
Do you…

425
00:35:25,015 --> 00:35:27,005
love me more than your God?

426
00:35:32,985 --> 00:35:34,005
More.

427
00:35:35,925 --> 00:35:37,205
More than anything.

428
00:35:38,155 --> 00:35:39,905
More than my own life.

429
00:36:16,175 --> 00:36:17,405
I love you, Mom.

430
00:36:51,195 --> 00:36:52,195
Barth.

431
00:36:52,225 --> 00:36:54,505
Let me use the bathroom real quick.

432
00:36:55,485 --> 00:36:56,485
Okay.

433
00:39:53,795 --> 00:39:55,285
College life looks fun?

434
00:39:55,435 --> 00:39:56,435
Don’t you think?

435
00:39:58,925 --> 00:39:59,925
Yeah.

436
00:40:01,515 --> 00:40:04,505
Just thinking about it is fun, isn’t it?

437
00:40:07,685 --> 00:40:08,685
Yeah.

438
00:40:10,155 --> 00:40:11,305
But I think

439
00:40:12,935 --> 00:40:14,405
college isn’t for me.

440
00:40:16,885 --> 00:40:18,805
I probably couldn’t even pass
the entrance exam.

441
00:40:19,285 --> 00:40:20,805
And even if I did,

442
00:40:21,405 --> 00:40:24,805
I wouldn’t have money for tuition anyway.

443
00:40:25,635 --> 00:40:27,305
Plus food and rent.

444
00:40:30,005 --> 00:40:32,805
But if I could,
I’d probably go to trade school,

445
00:40:33,925 --> 00:40:35,105
study for a year,

446
00:40:37,465 --> 00:40:39,205
then get a job and make some money.

447
00:40:44,395 --> 00:40:45,395
What about you?

448
00:40:46,105 --> 00:40:47,305
What do you want to study?

449
00:40:53,955 --> 00:40:54,955
I…

450
00:40:55,625 --> 00:40:56,805
I really don’t know.

451
00:40:57,435 --> 00:40:59,115
I mean, I honestly have no idea.

452
00:41:00,605 --> 00:41:03,305
If I try to picture anything else,
I can’t see it at all.

453
00:41:04,205 --> 00:41:07,205
I grew up at Magdalene House.

454
00:41:08,215 --> 00:41:09,905
If I had to choose another path,

455
00:41:10,695 --> 00:41:12,005
I don’t think I’d know how.

456
00:41:16,595 --> 00:41:17,595
Yeah.

457
00:41:36,265 --> 00:41:40,395
KANCHANABURI NONG PRUE

458
00:41:44,505 --> 00:41:46,005
Two for the 7 p.m. bus, please.

459
00:41:46,335 --> 00:41:48,505
Oh, the 7 p.m. bus is full.

460
00:41:51,005 --> 00:41:55,705
The earliest would be tomorrow at 6 a.m.

461
00:41:57,825 --> 00:41:58,605
What now?

462
00:41:58,675 --> 00:41:59,905
It’s not until 6 tomorrow.

463
00:42:01,635 --> 00:42:03,705
We’ll have to find somewhere
to sleep tonight.

464
00:42:05,535 --> 00:42:06,535
Come on.

465
00:42:14,135 --> 00:42:15,135
Hey, boys.

466
00:42:16,955 --> 00:42:19,275
There’s a cheap motel
in the alley over there.

467
00:42:19,685 --> 00:42:22,205
But the vibe’s a little weird.

468
00:43:02,155 --> 00:43:03,155
Oh!

469
00:43:07,985 --> 00:43:08,985
Hey!

470
00:43:32,905 --> 00:43:35,955
I think it’s okay.

471
00:43:37,375 --> 00:43:38,505
It’s only 300 baht.

472
00:43:51,775 --> 00:43:53,405
I’m gonna go buy something.

473
00:43:54,325 --> 00:43:55,325
You want anything?

474
00:44:11,615 --> 00:44:12,805
Try it if you want.

475
00:44:15,195 --> 00:44:16,705
One puff won’t kill you.

476
00:44:42,695 --> 00:44:44,205
What’s so great about this?

477
00:44:44,905 --> 00:44:46,705
Why do people like smoking so much?

478
00:44:49,485 --> 00:44:51,405
My dad said it helps with stress.

479
00:44:52,445 --> 00:44:55,105
Like, when you smoke,
your mind goes blank or something.

480
00:44:55,195 --> 00:44:56,195
Yeah.

481
00:44:56,545 --> 00:44:57,545
You try it.

482
00:44:57,925 --> 00:44:59,105
Maybe you’ll feel lighter.

483
00:45:13,445 --> 00:45:14,445
There.

484
00:45:14,655 --> 00:45:15,655
Feel lighter?

485
00:45:16,715 --> 00:45:17,875
More stressed than before.

486
00:45:24,085 --> 00:45:25,285
Screw it.

487
00:45:37,985 --> 00:45:39,585
I don’t want tomorrow to come.

488
00:45:41,455 --> 00:45:42,455
Yeah.

489
00:45:42,735 --> 00:45:43,805
Me neither.

490
00:45:48,185 --> 00:45:50,605
So what are you gonna do next?

491
00:45:56,195 --> 00:45:57,305
I still don’t know.

492
00:46:25,285 --> 00:46:30,805
Amidst the rainfall.

493
00:46:32,195 --> 00:46:37,775
This lonely heart of mine
comes back to life.

494
00:46:38,925 --> 00:46:44,605
All the things I never held dear.

495
00:46:45,905 --> 00:46:49,515
BARTH

496
00:46:51,415 --> 00:46:54,185
The stars had never shone for me.

497
00:46:54,215 --> 00:46:57,305
No beauty in their light.

498
00:46:58,135 --> 00:47:00,225
For the first time, they bloomed.

499
00:47:00,255 --> 00:47:04,705
When I met you, they came alive.

500
00:47:05,115 --> 00:47:11,275
The same old world feels new again.

501
00:47:11,625 --> 00:47:17,205
Today you help me understand.

502
00:47:17,955 --> 00:47:20,405
Every melody of a love song.

503
00:47:20,425 --> 00:47:22,335
Playing in my heart.

504
00:47:22,365 --> 00:47:25,605
Would never sound so beautiful.

505
00:47:25,745 --> 00:47:31,555
Without you, next to me, never apart.

506
00:47:31,765 --> 00:47:34,245
This song belongs to you and me.

507
00:47:34,275 --> 00:47:35,905
To us only.

508
00:47:35,935 --> 00:47:38,185
The sound inside has changed.

509
00:47:38,205 --> 00:47:40,405
It will never be the same.

510
00:47:40,695 --> 00:47:42,065
Because you.

511
00:47:42,405 --> 00:47:43,775
Because you.

512
00:47:43,995 --> 00:47:48,095
Fill my heart with the sound of love.

513
00:47:51,485 --> 00:47:58,005
Fill my heart with the sound of love.

514
00:47:58,025 --> 00:47:59,475
PARADISE

515
00:48:02,685 --> 00:48:03,685
Are you asleep?

516
00:48:07,855 --> 00:48:08,855
Yeah.

517
00:48:14,225 --> 00:48:15,605
Then how are you answering me?

518
00:48:19,635 --> 00:48:20,805
Are you teasing me?

519
00:48:21,525 --> 00:48:22,525
Hm?

520
00:48:30,625 --> 00:48:34,805
Well, you were acting all serious
when we first came in.

521
00:48:38,185 --> 00:48:39,185
Barth.

522
00:48:42,055 --> 00:48:43,205
I'm going to sleep.

523
00:48:52,795 --> 00:48:54,515
I was just scared you’d change your mind.

524
00:48:59,485 --> 00:49:00,505
Are you sure?

525
00:49:05,155 --> 00:49:06,155
What about you?

526
00:49:11,795 --> 00:49:12,795
Yeah.

527
00:49:25,055 --> 00:49:26,055
Tanrak.

528
00:49:27,465 --> 00:49:28,465
What’s wrong?

529
00:49:28,965 --> 00:49:30,105
What? Are you shy?

530
00:49:31,605 --> 00:49:32,605
Hm.

531
00:49:32,655 --> 00:49:33,795
- You’re shy?
- Hm.

532
00:49:34,055 --> 00:49:35,205
What are you doing? Huh?

533
00:49:50,555 --> 00:49:51,575
I…

534
00:49:53,135 --> 00:49:54,505
I love you, Tanrak.

535
00:49:56,795 --> 00:49:58,205
I love you too.

536
00:53:15,125 --> 00:53:16,125
Tanrak.

537
00:53:40,855 --> 00:53:42,505
It took so long to get here.

538
00:53:45,375 --> 00:53:47,405
If the calling wasn’t strong enough,

539
00:53:48,205 --> 00:53:49,745
he wouldn’t have made it this far.

540
00:53:53,885 --> 00:53:54,885
That’s true.

541
00:53:57,125 --> 00:53:58,505
It really has been a long time.

542
00:54:00,985 --> 00:54:03,505
Talking about it makes me miss those days.

543
00:54:05,535 --> 00:54:06,535
But…

544
00:54:06,695 --> 00:54:08,705
we can’t go back and change anything now.

545
00:54:19,885 --> 00:54:20,885
Father.

546
00:54:26,065 --> 00:54:27,355
Feel free to look around, Barth.

547
00:54:27,415 --> 00:54:28,505
We’ll talk later.

548
00:54:28,915 --> 00:54:29,915
Okay.

549
00:54:44,635 --> 00:54:46,115
All right, that should do it.

550
00:54:46,435 --> 00:54:48,905
Go pack up. The ceremony’s about to start.

551
00:54:49,425 --> 00:54:50,425
Go on.

552
00:54:52,655 --> 00:54:54,005
- Hello, Master Phak.
- Barth!

553
00:54:56,115 --> 00:54:57,715
I guess I can’t call you Master anymore.

554
00:54:58,235 --> 00:54:59,405
Hello, Father Phak.

555
00:55:01,165 --> 00:55:02,405
You can just call me Phak.

556
00:55:02,865 --> 00:55:03,865
I don’t mind.

557
00:55:05,845 --> 00:55:06,935
Better not.

558
00:55:07,695 --> 00:55:08,905
You’re a priest now.

559
00:55:09,045 --> 00:55:10,195
It wouldn’t be proper.

560
00:55:13,795 --> 00:55:15,685
But he’s really steadfast, isn’t he?

561
00:55:16,885 --> 00:55:20,205
Out of our whole class,
he’s the only one left.

562
00:55:22,335 --> 00:55:23,905
Not “only one left.”

563
00:55:24,815 --> 00:55:26,485
One person made it all the way.

564
00:55:27,765 --> 00:55:29,905
It's been a long road to get here.

565
00:55:30,705 --> 00:55:33,685
Those who left along the way
did nothing wrong.

566
00:55:48,395 --> 00:55:49,805
They really did nothing wrong?

567
00:55:58,245 --> 00:56:00,405
There’s no such thing
as the “right” life, Barth.

568
00:56:01,665 --> 00:56:05,105
Every life has its own path.

569
00:56:06,525 --> 00:56:08,635
God always gives us the chance to choose.

570
00:56:09,535 --> 00:56:11,605
As long as we remain in His love.

571
00:56:15,965 --> 00:56:18,745
So how have you two been?

572
00:56:49,145 --> 00:56:50,145
Father.

573
00:56:56,095 --> 00:56:57,685
I have something to confess.

574
00:57:04,415 --> 00:57:06,605
What would you like to confess, my child?

575
00:57:26,535 --> 00:57:27,805
I’ve sinned.

576
00:57:33,915 --> 00:57:35,605
I wronged the people who helped me.

577
00:57:40,605 --> 00:57:42,005
I sinned against God.

578
00:57:45,415 --> 00:57:46,905
I betrayed everyone

579
00:57:48,775 --> 00:57:50,205
who trusted me.

580
00:57:53,355 --> 00:57:54,705
Everyone

581
00:57:56,705 --> 00:57:58,405
who gave me a chance.

582
00:58:02,235 --> 00:58:03,235
Father.

583
00:58:07,005 --> 00:58:08,205
I’m scared.

584
00:58:14,135 --> 00:58:15,985
I’m scared I won’t go to heaven.

585
00:58:19,595 --> 00:58:20,595
I’m scared.

586
00:58:22,805 --> 00:58:24,605
I won’t get to see Him anymore.

587
00:58:30,845 --> 00:58:32,505
Don’t worry, my child.

588
00:58:33,675 --> 00:58:36,005
God always gives you another chance.

589
00:58:37,395 --> 00:58:39,755
As long as you’re truly sorry,

590
00:58:40,105 --> 00:58:41,405
that’s enough.

591
00:58:43,545 --> 00:58:44,655
God

592
00:58:45,965 --> 00:58:48,085
is still waiting for you in heaven.

593
00:58:49,335 --> 00:58:51,005
Your parents

594
00:58:52,535 --> 00:58:54,605
are still waiting for you there too.

595
00:59:00,385 --> 00:59:01,385
Father.

596
00:59:05,065 --> 00:59:06,405
You know it’s me.

597
00:59:10,305 --> 00:59:12,005
Don’t worry, my child.

598
00:59:13,235 --> 00:59:15,505
Even if you’re not ordained,

599
00:59:16,495 --> 00:59:17,805
God

600
00:59:18,905 --> 00:59:21,505
can still live in your heart.

601
00:59:29,045 --> 00:59:32,805
He will remain there

602
00:59:34,005 --> 00:59:35,805
with you forever.

603
00:59:49,715 --> 00:59:50,805
It’s okay.

604
00:59:51,655 --> 00:59:52,655
Tanrak.

605
00:59:58,245 --> 00:59:59,245
It's okay.

606
01:00:18,675 --> 01:00:19,675
It's okay.

607
01:00:28,575 --> 01:00:29,575
Father.

608
01:00:30,305 --> 01:00:31,335
I’m sorry.

609
01:00:32,915 --> 01:00:34,705
I feel so selfish.

610
01:00:37,565 --> 01:00:38,705
It’s okay.

611
01:00:39,975 --> 01:00:41,475
It’s okay, Tanrak.

612
01:00:44,935 --> 01:00:47,005
You need to forgive yourself.

613
01:00:48,315 --> 01:00:52,205
You’ve carried this long enough.

614
01:00:56,545 --> 01:00:59,585
You don’t have to carry it
for the rest of your life.

615
01:02:34,295 --> 01:02:35,975
Back when I was still a student,

616
01:02:36,795 --> 01:02:39,775
many things taught me

617
01:02:40,885 --> 01:02:42,105
about the good things,

618
01:02:42,575 --> 01:02:43,805
the disappointments,

619
01:02:44,395 --> 01:02:45,505
the failures,

620
01:02:46,145 --> 01:02:47,145
love,

621
01:02:48,115 --> 01:02:49,505
and friendship.

622
01:02:50,835 --> 01:02:53,405
And three things always remain.

623
01:02:54,425 --> 01:02:55,425
Those are

624
01:02:56,105 --> 01:02:57,105
faith,

625
01:02:58,465 --> 01:02:59,505
hope,

626
01:03:00,965 --> 01:03:02,015
and love.

627
01:03:09,675 --> 01:03:10,895
And love

628
01:03:11,795 --> 01:03:13,105
is the greatest of all.

629
01:03:41,675 --> 01:03:42,675
Tanrak.

630
01:03:44,425 --> 01:03:46,005
I just ran into Father Phak.

631
01:03:47,255 --> 01:03:48,605
He asked about us.

632
01:03:50,825 --> 01:03:51,825
Really?

633
01:03:53,435 --> 01:03:54,705
What did you tell him?

634
01:03:58,705 --> 01:03:59,905
I told him,

635
01:04:02,205 --> 01:04:03,505
"I put him through a lot."

636
01:04:06,705 --> 01:04:09,355
We had to work for years
before we could go to college.

637
01:04:11,365 --> 01:04:12,405
Studying,

638
01:04:13,285 --> 01:04:14,485
working,

639
01:04:17,265 --> 01:04:18,605
trying to pay tuition.

640
01:04:21,805 --> 01:04:22,885
It wasn’t easy.

641
01:04:25,275 --> 01:04:26,485
But…

642
01:04:29,575 --> 01:04:30,575
But what?

643
01:04:41,475 --> 01:04:43,255
But we never let go of each other

644
01:04:45,115 --> 01:04:46,805
from that day until now.

645
01:04:53,335 --> 01:04:54,335
Well,

646
01:04:55,675 --> 01:04:57,205
I tried to shake you off.

647
01:04:58,745 --> 01:05:00,305
But you just wouldn’t come loose.

648
01:05:06,265 --> 01:05:07,905
Who was it that told me this?

649
01:05:10,175 --> 01:05:11,605
"No matter where I am,

650
01:05:13,125 --> 01:05:15,305
as long as you're next to me,
everything's fine."

651
01:05:31,715 --> 01:05:34,105
Do you remember
how I used to tease you all the time?

652
01:05:35,425 --> 01:05:36,425
I’d say,

653
01:05:37,835 --> 01:05:39,475
“Do you really believe in God?”

654
01:05:42,655 --> 01:05:43,655
Of course I remember.

655
01:05:43,905 --> 01:05:45,105
How could I not?

656
01:05:45,615 --> 01:05:47,205
You teased me every day.

657
01:05:53,795 --> 01:05:55,205
Back then, I thought

658
01:05:59,105 --> 01:06:00,405
if God was real,

659
01:06:03,425 --> 01:06:05,205
He probably didn’t care much about me.

660
01:06:09,325 --> 01:06:11,405
But thinking about it now,

661
01:06:15,185 --> 01:06:16,305
I feel like

662
01:06:17,705 --> 01:06:19,205
no matter what I did,

663
01:06:21,945 --> 01:06:24,085
He never disappeared from my life.

664
01:06:28,235 --> 01:06:29,405
Without Him,

665
01:06:32,345 --> 01:06:33,685
I wouldn’t have met you.

666
01:06:36,195 --> 01:06:37,705
And we wouldn’t have today.

667
01:06:39,635 --> 01:06:40,635
Well, I…

668
01:06:42,155 --> 01:06:43,405
I used to think

669
01:06:44,355 --> 01:06:45,685
after meeting you,

670
01:06:46,405 --> 01:06:47,405
I had to choose.

671
01:06:48,965 --> 01:06:50,005
But actually,

672
01:06:50,775 --> 01:06:52,035
I never had to choose at all.

673
01:06:58,575 --> 01:07:01,905
Because ever since you came into my life,

674
01:07:03,355 --> 01:07:05,305
I never forgot God either.

675
01:07:37,705 --> 01:07:39,225
EUCHARISTIC CELEBRATION
AND PRIESTLY ORDINATION

676
01:07:39,245 --> 01:07:40,485
DEACON JOSEPH KONGDECH SAENKHAM

677
01:07:47,145 --> 01:07:48,145
Ahem.

678
01:07:49,605 --> 01:07:51,405
Hello, Father Kongdech.

679
01:07:54,775 --> 01:07:55,775
Are you messing with me?

680
01:07:58,035 --> 01:07:59,705
Just call me Kongdech like before.

681
01:08:00,455 --> 01:08:01,775
We’re still friends.

682
01:08:02,535 --> 01:08:04,405
Just maybe skip the rude pronouns.

683
01:08:06,605 --> 01:08:10,505
I just wanted to say

684
01:08:11,055 --> 01:08:13,395
thank you for remembering my first sermon.

685
01:08:14,435 --> 01:08:15,435
Of course I remember.

686
01:08:17,025 --> 01:08:18,405
I don’t have many friends.

687
01:08:18,745 --> 01:08:20,105
So whatever anyone says,

688
01:08:20,485 --> 01:08:21,685
I remember it all.

689
01:08:25,985 --> 01:08:29,675
Thank you so much, dear Father,
for still calling me your friend.

690
01:08:32,795 --> 01:08:34,105
Want to talk like old times?

691
01:08:34,685 --> 01:08:35,805
Might make you less nervous.

692
01:08:35,915 --> 01:08:39,505
You’re so tense it’s painful to watch.

693
01:08:39,645 --> 01:08:40,345
Okay, okay.

694
01:08:40,385 --> 01:08:41,775
What? Are you crazy?

695
01:08:41,865 --> 01:08:43,465
You can’t talk to a priest like that.

696
01:08:44,355 --> 01:08:45,555
That’s hell-worthy.

697
01:08:47,815 --> 01:08:48,815
Barth.

698
01:08:51,595 --> 01:08:52,755
Look at his robe.

699
01:08:54,515 --> 01:08:55,515
Father.

700
01:08:56,875 --> 01:08:58,605
Sorry, there’s something on you.

701
01:08:59,755 --> 01:09:00,755
What is it?

702
01:09:01,695 --> 01:09:04,305
Oh, gray hair.

703
01:09:06,565 --> 01:09:07,565
You’re old now.

704
01:09:09,985 --> 01:09:10,985
Yes, my child.

705
01:09:11,665 --> 01:09:12,795
Hell is hot, you know.

706
01:09:13,255 --> 01:09:16,005
Don’t forget to bring cooling powder
when you fall in.

707
01:09:37,725 --> 01:09:40,405
I’m happy for you, man.

708
01:09:42,155 --> 01:09:43,155
Oops.

709
01:09:43,885 --> 01:09:46,805
I’m happy for you, Father Kongdech.

710
01:09:48,345 --> 01:09:51,305
Thank you, my child Tanrak.

711
01:09:53,935 --> 01:09:55,555
Please hear my confession too.

712
01:09:56,195 --> 01:09:57,905
I'll book you a month in advance.

713
01:09:58,295 --> 01:10:00,295
I have a feeling
you have a lot of sins to confess.

714
01:10:00,415 --> 01:10:01,415
My child, Barth.

715
01:10:10,125 --> 01:10:11,125
Father.

716
01:10:11,295 --> 01:10:13,975
I’m sorry, and thank you again
for everything.

717
01:10:15,975 --> 01:10:17,505
Love yourself more.

718
01:10:18,115 --> 01:10:20,625
And if you get the chance,
come back and visit me sometime.

719
01:10:59,815 --> 01:11:00,815
Hey, Tan.

720
01:11:03,015 --> 01:11:04,105
If we get ordained,

721
01:11:04,935 --> 01:11:07,605
what would your first sermon be about?

722
01:11:11,135 --> 01:11:12,505
I want to preach about

723
01:11:12,865 --> 01:11:17,205
love, faith, and hope from Corinthians.

724
01:11:18,485 --> 01:11:19,205
Why?

725
01:11:19,282 --> 01:11:24,405
Turn into memories I treasure for life.

726
01:11:24,812 --> 01:11:27,537
The stars had never shone for me.

727
01:11:27,575 --> 01:11:30,635
No beauty in their light.

728
01:11:31,501 --> 01:11:33,605
For the first time, they bloomed.

729
01:11:33,625 --> 01:11:37,797
When I met you, they came alive.

730
01:11:38,486 --> 01:11:44,705
The same old world feels new again.

731
01:11:45,007 --> 01:11:50,489
Today you help me understand.

732
01:11:51,353 --> 01:11:53,735
Every melody of a love song.

733
01:11:53,756 --> 01:11:55,504
Playing in my heart.

734
01:11:55,625 --> 01:11:58,605
Humans can live without faith.

735
01:12:00,465 --> 01:12:02,705
Humans can live without hope.

736
01:12:04,045 --> 01:12:07,505
But humans cannot live without love.

737
01:12:09,645 --> 01:12:11,205
Even without faith,

738
01:12:11,825 --> 01:12:13,775
if humans love deeply enough,

739
01:12:14,275 --> 01:12:15,595
they will believe.

740
01:12:20,655 --> 01:12:22,105
Even without hope,

741
01:12:22,785 --> 01:12:24,835
if humans love deeply enough,

742
01:12:25,675 --> 01:12:27,005
they will hope.

743
01:12:28,505 --> 01:12:30,605
But without love,

744
01:12:31,235 --> 01:12:34,255
humans have no chance of finding Him.

745
01:12:37,235 --> 01:12:40,705
God’s love is everything.

746
01:12:42,015 --> 01:12:43,635
It is love for oneself.

747
01:12:44,555 --> 01:12:46,605
It is love for one’s neighbor.

748
01:12:51,845 --> 01:12:55,605
For He created all things.

749
01:12:57,455 --> 01:12:58,705
Wherever there is love,

750
01:12:59,395 --> 01:13:02,205
He is always present there.

751
01:13:05,535 --> 01:13:07,915
Love is therefore the most important

752
01:13:08,685 --> 01:13:10,105
and the greatest of all.

753
01:13:12,935 --> 01:13:16,505
Because love is never without Him.

754
01:13:16,525 --> 01:13:17,525
THE END

755
01:13:17,566 --> 01:13:20,600
The same old world feels new again.

756
01:13:21,033 --> 01:13:26,488
Today you help me understand.

757
01:13:27,324 --> 01:13:29,733
Every melody of a love song.

758
01:13:29,755 --> 01:13:31,515
Playing in my heart.

759
01:13:31,691 --> 01:13:35,005
Would never sound so beautiful.

760
01:13:35,098 --> 01:13:40,886
Without you, next to me, never apart.

761
01:13:41,123 --> 01:13:43,567
This song belongs to you and me.

762
01:13:43,641 --> 01:13:45,270
To us only.

763
01:13:45,315 --> 01:13:47,529
The sound inside has changed.

764
01:13:47,545 --> 01:13:49,733
It will never be the same.

765
01:13:50,135 --> 01:13:51,405
Because you.

766
01:13:51,805 --> 01:13:53,167
Because you.

767
01:13:53,355 --> 01:13:58,206
Fill my heart with the sound of love.

768
01:14:00,844 --> 01:14:07,288
Fill my heart with the sound of love.

769
01:14:30,875 --> 01:14:32,005
Took you long enough.

770
01:14:33,575 --> 01:14:34,605
Tired today?

771
01:14:36,115 --> 01:14:37,805
Two of my staff quit today.

772
01:14:38,955 --> 01:14:40,075
Way more tiring than usual.

773
01:14:43,915 --> 01:14:45,055
I’m sore all over.

774
01:14:47,795 --> 01:14:48,795
Hold onto this for me.

775
01:14:51,925 --> 01:14:52,925
Barth.

776
01:14:54,275 --> 01:14:56,235
Why are you getting into bed
without showering?

777
01:14:56,255 --> 01:14:57,255
You stink.

778
01:14:57,465 --> 01:14:59,305
Let me lie down for a second. I’m tired.

779
01:15:00,375 --> 01:15:01,375
Please.

780
01:15:02,055 --> 01:15:03,305
So tired.

781
01:15:04,345 --> 01:15:05,055
Go shower.

782
01:15:05,075 --> 01:15:06,795
I’m really tired. Just a second.

783
01:15:07,245 --> 01:15:09,105
Just a second. Just a second.

784
01:15:11,595 --> 01:15:13,675
Hurry up and shower
before this becomes a habit.

785
01:15:20,375 --> 01:15:21,705
Still nagging like always.

786
01:15:27,655 --> 01:15:29,155
One minute, Rak.

787
01:15:30,685 --> 01:15:31,955
You stink.

788
01:15:49,165 --> 01:15:51,205
You must really like this necklace.

789
01:15:52,225 --> 01:15:53,275
You wear it every day.

790
01:15:57,535 --> 01:16:03,305
I went from being Mom’s beloved

791
01:16:04,675 --> 01:16:05,905
to being…

792
01:16:06,345 --> 01:16:07,605
beloved by…

793
01:16:09,765 --> 01:16:10,765
By who?

794
01:16:13,915 --> 01:16:15,905
God.

795
01:16:26,105 --> 01:16:27,105
Or you?

796
01:16:29,555 --> 01:16:31,205
Of course you’re Barth’s.

797
01:16:39,335 --> 01:16:40,335
You know,

798
01:16:40,735 --> 01:16:42,405
I used to think.

799
01:16:42,855 --> 01:16:44,395
God probably didn’t love me much.

800
01:16:45,775 --> 01:16:46,775
Why?

801
01:16:49,465 --> 01:16:50,705
Look at my life back then.

802
01:16:51,065 --> 01:16:52,065
It was a total mess.

803
01:16:53,255 --> 01:16:55,805
It felt like He had forgotten me.

804
01:16:58,745 --> 01:17:01,945
But He sent you to meet me.

805
01:17:06,335 --> 01:17:08,315
Why does that sound like a punishment?

806
01:17:09,955 --> 01:17:10,955
It’s not.

807
01:17:12,425 --> 01:17:13,605
To me,

808
01:17:14,605 --> 01:17:15,905
it’s a miracle.

809
01:17:31,945 --> 01:17:36,405
You’re Barth’s one and only beloved.

810
01:17:42,445 --> 01:17:43,445
Aren’t you?

811
01:18:03,285 --> 01:18:04,285
Am I?

812
01:18:08,635 --> 01:18:10,605
Now I’ve got the motivation to shower.

813
01:18:12,005 --> 01:18:13,805
I’m gonna shower. Be right back.

814
01:18:17,515 --> 01:18:18,515
Hey.

815
01:18:33,335 --> 01:18:37,285
Come back for more kisses
after your shower.

816
01:18:41,725 --> 01:18:42,955
I’ll shower really fast.

817
01:18:58,595 --> 01:18:59,855
I don’t wanna shower anymore.

818
01:19:00,595 --> 01:19:01,705
I wanna stay right here.

819
01:19:01,935 --> 01:19:03,905
Weren’t you going to shower?

820
01:19:04,495 --> 01:19:05,805
Barth.

821
01:19:06,115 --> 01:19:07,005
One second.

822
01:19:07,125 --> 01:19:08,005
You stink.

823
01:19:08,025 --> 01:19:09,155
Let me lie here first.

824
01:19:09,175 --> 01:19:10,605
Go lie on your own side.

825
01:19:11,075 --> 01:19:12,075
Come here.

826
01:19:12,715 --> 01:19:13,715
Come on.

827
01:19:14,155 --> 01:19:15,205
Come with me.

828
01:19:15,475 --> 01:19:16,475
Hey, Barth.

829
01:19:16,935 --> 01:19:17,935
Barth.

830
01:19:18,675 --> 01:19:19,805
Just stay for a second.

831
01:19:21,155 --> 01:19:22,155
Just a second.

832
01:19:22,255 --> 01:19:23,255
Just a second.

833
01:19:26,095 --> 01:19:27,095
Come on.

834
01:19:36,195 --> 01:19:38,485
Every second From that moment.

835
01:19:38,505 --> 01:19:40,799
That I have you near.

836
01:19:40,814 --> 01:19:44,905
Feels like I’ve found
the land of my dreams.

837
01:19:45,235 --> 01:19:50,405
My world turns so beautiful
I wanna stop the time.

838
01:19:50,425 --> 01:19:53,846
TAN…RAK

839
01:19:53,865 --> 01:19:56,215
If heaven is real
If it’s not real

840
